A random generator for each game (Commander Duels v0.8.5), in every format.

Reason: XMage draws every random number (shuffles, coin flips, random choices, AI tie-breaks) from
one process-wide java.util.Random, and RandomUtil.setSeed reseeds it. With several games in one
process, starting a game reset the stream the others were drawing from, so a seed no longer
repeated a game, and a game started with a known seed put every running game on a known stream.
With this patch setSeed gives the calling thread a generator of its own; that thread's draws come
from it alone, and threads that never seeded one share an unseeded generator as before. A game's
loop runs on the thread that started it, which is the thread the engine seeds.
Upstream: none.
Remove when: XMage keeps a random generator per game.

